1
00:01:40,879 --> 00:01:42,599
Back when the old lady lived in the village,

2
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,120
that was why you all went back.

3
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:45,519
Now that she's gone,

4
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:49,120
who would ever go back to live there?

5
00:01:51,239 --> 00:01:54,079
All the young people want to move to the city.

6
00:01:54,400 --> 00:01:56,680
Nobody wants the old house even for free.

7
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:59,400
You couldn't beg them to return.

8
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,599
Right now in the village,

9
00:02:00,599 --> 00:02:02,319
only Old Fifth is left.

10
00:02:02,319 --> 00:02:05,280
So let's just give the old house to him.

11
00:02:06,719 --> 00:02:08,439
To be honest,

12
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:11,199
he might not even live in an old house like this.

13
00:02:11,199 --> 00:02:14,639
At most, he'd store some rice and vegetables there.

14
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:16,280
At least he can look after the place.

15
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:18,199
If we hire someone else to look after it,

16
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:19,280
we'd have to pay them.

17
00:02:19,479 --> 00:02:22,199
That leaves the matter of the farmland.

18
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:24,199
Certainly no one is going to farm it,

19
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:25,680
unless it's rented out.

20
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,199
Why don't we just

21
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,080
give it all to Old Fifth?

22
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,439
Otherwise, which of you wants to deal with this hassle?

23
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:36,879
Yeah, that's true.

24
00:02:36,879 --> 00:02:39,280
If no one has any objections,

25
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,879
then let's settle it like this.

26
00:02:41,560 --> 00:02:44,159
What do you mean by that?

27
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:46,319
The house is given away,

28
00:02:46,319 --> 00:02:47,280
the land is given away,

29
00:02:47,759 --> 00:02:48,759
all to Fifth Uncle?

30
00:02:50,039 --> 00:02:51,800
And her? She gets nothing?

31
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:54,039
She already divorced you.

32
00:02:54,199 --> 00:02:55,039
Since they're divorced,

33
00:02:59,120 --> 00:03:00,120
she's just an outsider.

34
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:01,639
Now you bring up the divorce?

35
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:03,520
She took care of my mother every day,

36
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,039
stayed by her hospital bed every year,

37
00:03:05,039 --> 00:03:06,199
and exhausted herself into the hospital.

38
00:03:06,199 --> 00:03:08,120
Why didn't you mention the divorce back then?

39
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,280
What about you all? What did you ever do for her?

40
00:03:11,800 --> 00:03:13,319
You just wanted to snatch her bracelets.

41
00:03:13,319 --> 00:03:15,080
Did any of you visit her in the hospital?

42
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:18,120
Did anyone share a single vegetable leaf?

43
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:20,159
Did any of you elders do that?

44
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,319
So what do you want?

45
00:03:27,719 --> 00:03:28,680
Go ahead and speak.

46
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,039
My opinion is,

47
00:03:32,960 --> 00:03:34,159
giving it all to Fifth Uncle is fine.

48
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,080
Second Uncle is right too.

49
00:03:36,159 --> 00:03:37,520
Who would ever come back to live here?

50
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:40,000
But we have to be fair about this.

51
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:41,439
You decide on the house.

52
00:03:41,439 --> 00:03:43,680
However, the loquat tree behind the house

53
00:03:44,800 --> 00:03:45,560
must stay.

54
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:48,039
Yazhen planted it the year she married in.

55
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,280
If the house isn't hers,

56
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,680
the tree should at least belong to her.

57
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:54,520
Its fruit every year should be hers too.

58
00:03:56,199 --> 00:03:57,520
Fine, fine, fine.

59
00:03:57,639 --> 00:03:58,120
Is that fine?

60
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,120
All right.

61
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,319
We'll do as you say.

62
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:01,879
Let's get going, then.

63
00:04:01,879 --> 00:04:02,840
Let them talk it over.

64
00:04:03,479 --> 00:04:04,439
Let's go, let's go.

65
00:04:32,879 --> 00:04:34,319
I wired the money to your dad yesterday.

66
00:04:35,279 --> 00:04:37,079
Sent all my savings from the past years.

67
00:04:37,399 --> 00:04:38,639
Tell him to take those unfinished rooms

68
00:04:38,639 --> 00:04:39,480
and get them rebuilt properly.

69
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:40,639
Hire people to do the work.

70
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:43,240
Don't let him do anything where he'd fall.

71
00:04:46,519 --> 00:04:48,240
And about your brother's kid going to college,

72
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:49,240
I've looked into that, too.

73
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:50,560
With scores that low,

74
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:51,439
special admission is the only way.

75
00:04:52,319 --> 00:04:53,199
Just wait to hear from me.

76
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:56,079
Understood.

77
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:08,199
My mom left this for you.

78
00:05:31,199 --> 00:05:32,399
In the years before our divorce,

79
00:05:34,439 --> 00:05:35,560
I was always on the move,

80
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:36,519
never there for you.

81
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,279
I thought getting divorced

82
00:05:40,480 --> 00:05:41,560
would stop holding you back.

83
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:45,879
But then, because of my mother,

84
00:05:46,639 --> 00:05:47,920
I held you back for so many more years.

85
00:05:51,439 --> 00:05:53,279
Maybe everyone has their own fate.

86
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,360
Maybe by nature,

87
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:58,680
I'm like a wild horse,

88
00:05:59,279 --> 00:06:00,439
meant to roam alone,

89
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:03,639
not cut out for a normal life.

90
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,800
I owe you.

91
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,720
When I was a kid,

92
00:06:34,720 --> 00:06:36,240
I really wanted to have a pet,

93
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:37,920
but my family wouldn't let me.

94
00:06:38,519 --> 00:06:39,759
Our neighbors had so many—

95
00:06:40,199 --> 00:06:42,680
cats, dogs,

96
00:06:42,680 --> 00:06:44,920
rabbits, and birds.

97
00:06:45,199 --> 00:06:46,439
It was like a zoo.

98
00:06:47,519 --> 00:06:49,439
I'd peer through their door every day,

99
00:06:49,639 --> 00:06:51,759
watching the little animals eat

100
00:06:51,759 --> 00:06:53,000
and watching them drink.

101
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:57,879
What medication are you taking?

102
00:06:58,160 --> 00:07:00,000
For hypothyroidism or hyperthyroidism?

103
00:07:00,279 --> 00:07:02,199
Raise it first. Lower if it's too much,

104
00:07:02,199 --> 00:07:03,439
and raise it if it's too low.

105
00:07:13,399 --> 00:07:14,680
It was my fault today.

106
00:07:14,680 --> 00:07:15,519
I'm sorry.

107
00:07:16,399 --> 00:07:17,519
It's been happening a lot lately.

108
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,360
Losing my temper for no reason.

109
00:07:19,839 --> 00:07:21,079
I just can't control it.

110
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:22,839
How could anyone blame you?

111
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:24,759
Who can control their thyroid?

112
00:07:24,959 --> 00:07:26,680
Besides, you've always slept poorly.

113
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:27,759
Now that you're on medication,

114
00:07:27,759 --> 00:07:29,079
it'll get much better.

115
00:07:31,639 --> 00:07:33,000
Too many occupational hazards.

116
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,040
My hearing has gotten worse lately too.

117
00:07:36,199 --> 00:07:37,839
Working around the clock.

118
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:39,639
Ever since we moved in here,

119
00:07:39,639 --> 00:07:41,240
I can't even remember how long it's been.

120
00:07:41,399 --> 00:07:43,199
Think my temper's gotten warped too?

121
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,439
What about me?

122
00:07:44,759 --> 00:07:47,079
Have I changed much these past few years?

123
00:07:47,439 --> 00:07:48,439
I used to talk a lot.

124
00:07:48,959 --> 00:07:50,279
Now I speak less and less.

125
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,199
Will I end up completely mute?

126
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,600
Haven't heard you joke in a long time.

127
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:58,519
I've almost forgotten how to.

128
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,120
Speaking of wishful thinking,

129
00:08:01,639 --> 00:08:03,519
right now I just want to run out of this room.

130
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:04,600
Anywhere would do.

131
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:05,600
Any city would do.

132
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:06,680
Doing anything at all.

133
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:08,240
Even just finding a small stream

134
00:08:08,639 --> 00:08:10,000
and watching the little fish,

135
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:12,600
I feel like it'd clear my head.

136
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:15,199
By the way, you brought it back—

137
00:08:15,399 --> 00:08:16,480
does Qiu Tian know?

138
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:20,279
How have things been between you two?

139
00:08:20,600 --> 00:08:21,399
Going smoothly?

140
00:08:22,920 --> 00:08:25,519
Handling an asset is the hardest thing in the world.

141
00:08:25,519 --> 00:08:26,680
Aligning their mindset is even harder.

142
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:28,160
You have to ensure

143
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:30,199
her life and work stay just as before.

144
00:08:30,199 --> 00:08:31,720
There can't be any change.

145
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:33,000
Besides, if Qiu Tian

146
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,840
was previously registered on their roster,

147
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:37,000
Taiwan, China will run polygraphs on her.

148
00:08:37,240 --> 00:08:39,399
We don't know if she was ever registered.

149
00:08:39,399 --> 00:08:40,159
I asked her once.

150
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:41,159
She wouldn't say.

151
00:08:41,440 --> 00:08:43,320
Jin Chizhong scarred her too deeply.

152
00:08:43,840 --> 00:08:44,919
We can't push her too hard.

153
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:46,480
What about Lin Kanshan?

154
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:49,000
Have they been in touch much lately?

155
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,240
Not entirely sure.

156
00:08:50,799 --> 00:08:51,679
That's the problem.

157
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,879
Lin Kanshan has been going out a lot lately.

158
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,320
If Qiu Tian could—

159
00:09:01,919 --> 00:09:02,879
Qiu Tian's calling.

160
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:11,919
My chest feels tight.

161
00:09:12,559 --> 00:09:13,799
I can't catch my breath.

162
00:09:16,200 --> 00:09:17,159
I didn't bring enough medication.

163
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:19,840
I think

164
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,279
I'm having another episode.

165
00:09:21,919 --> 00:09:22,919
Don't panic.

166
00:09:22,919 --> 00:09:24,000
Take your time and talk to me.

167
00:09:26,799 --> 00:09:28,360
Don't dwell on negative thoughts.

168
00:09:28,679 --> 00:09:30,879
Dwelling on it only makes you feel worse.

169
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,840
It's okay. Don't worry.

170
00:09:33,200 --> 00:09:34,159
Take it slow.

171
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,240
Just like I said,

172
00:09:37,679 --> 00:09:39,000
don't fight it.

173
00:09:39,320 --> 00:09:40,840
Don't resist that feeling.

174
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:42,679
I know it's miserable right now,

175
00:09:42,919 --> 00:09:44,480
but can you try just once

176
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,679
to accept it?

177
00:09:47,279 --> 00:09:48,759
Just picture it as

178
00:09:49,639 --> 00:09:50,480
your cat.

179
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,720
Imagine it's a little animal

180
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,480
wandering inside from outdoors.

181
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,799
You don't need to chase or shoo it away.

182
00:09:57,799 --> 00:09:58,960
Just let it stay.

183
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:00,279
For as long as it wants.

184
00:10:00,879 --> 00:10:02,240
The more you chase and scare it,

185
00:10:02,679 --> 00:10:03,879
the more likely it is to tear up

186
00:10:03,879 --> 00:10:05,000
everything in your room.

187
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,559
The more you ignore it,

188
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,440
the quieter it gets, right?

189
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:09,399
It won't act up.

190
00:10:11,759 --> 00:10:13,080
Are you listening to me?

191
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,639
Can you keep talking?

192
00:10:16,440 --> 00:10:17,279
Right now,

193
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:19,240
I'm so scared right now.

194
00:10:21,399 --> 00:10:23,480
I don't even know what I'm afraid of.

195
00:10:25,799 --> 00:10:28,039
I just want to hear you say more.

196
00:10:29,559 --> 00:10:30,679
Anything at all.

197
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:34,080
It's just like my insomnia.

198
00:10:34,360 --> 00:10:35,600
The more I fear it

199
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,759
and try to push it away,

200
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:37,960
the more it lingers,

201
00:10:38,559 --> 00:10:39,480
closing in on you.

202
00:10:41,039 --> 00:10:42,759
So why not just open your arms,

203
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:44,200
embrace it,

204
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,399
and accept it?

205
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:46,840
Just let go.

206
00:10:47,559 --> 00:10:49,279
Then it won't seem nearly as scary.

207
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:52,159
Like eating chili peppers when we were kids.

208
00:10:52,679 --> 00:10:54,440
We were terrified before trying it,

209
00:10:55,039 --> 00:10:56,720
but once we took a bite,

210
00:10:57,159 --> 00:10:59,480
we saw it wasn't really that bad.

211
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:02,320
If it weren't for you,

212
00:11:05,879 --> 00:11:07,320
I wouldn't even be here anymore.

213
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:44,799
Give me a call if anything comes up.

214
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:55,919
Go inside and get some sleep.

215
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,200
I let my guard down.

216
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:20,720
These guys can really hold their liquor.

217
00:12:21,639 --> 00:12:23,480
Brought a whole case, and it's almost gone.

218
00:12:23,480 --> 00:12:25,159
Weren't they in the military before?

219
00:12:27,759 --> 00:12:29,679
You won't like hearing this,

220
00:12:29,679 --> 00:12:31,279
but if Brother Qi were here today,

221
00:12:31,559 --> 00:12:33,399
we would've won this round.

222
00:12:33,600 --> 00:12:35,279
What's he always doing abroad, anyway?

223
00:12:35,279 --> 00:12:37,200
The last time he came back was last year.

224
00:12:37,879 --> 00:12:39,399
Have you seen him since?

225
00:12:39,679 --> 00:12:41,200
He doesn't care for me.

226
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:43,399
Why embarrass myself sucking up to him?

227
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:46,320
Sending a wreath to pay my respects was enough.

228
00:12:46,799 --> 00:12:48,120
You're still relatives, after all.

229
00:12:48,919 --> 00:12:51,399
And brothers who built a business.

230
00:12:51,759 --> 00:12:53,639
Over some petty nonsense,

231
00:12:53,639 --> 00:12:54,919
you two completely fell out.

232
00:12:54,919 --> 00:12:55,960
It's just pointless.

233
00:12:56,799 --> 00:12:58,679
The beaten path was too narrow.

234
00:12:58,679 --> 00:13:00,720
Luckily, I took the risky path back then.

235
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:03,279
Otherwise, I'd still be a lousy driver.

236
00:13:03,360 --> 00:13:05,480
GM of Xinghui Medical Equipment?

237
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,600
Not a chance.

238
00:13:08,279 --> 00:13:09,879
Real estate is still the way to go.

239
00:13:09,879 --> 00:13:12,000
China's economic boom can't be stopped.

240
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,080
Pedal to the metal,

241
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:15,200
It'll outstrip Japan and South Korea.

242
00:13:15,200 --> 00:13:16,759
What do people do once they have money?

243
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,320
Those without homes buy homes.

244
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:19,720
Those with homes want to upgrade.

245
00:13:19,960 --> 00:13:21,720
Medical equipment has run its course.

246
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:22,879
Hit a dead end.

247
00:13:23,039 --> 00:13:23,919
Well, I have a small appetite anyway.

248
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:26,120
If the pie's too big, I can't stomach it.

249
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,120
You should really reconsider investing.

250
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:31,000
You say your appetite's small,

251
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:32,360
but I just lack the guts.

252
00:13:32,360 --> 00:13:34,080
Things like skyscrapers,

253
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:35,320
they sound terrifying to me.

254
00:13:35,679 --> 00:13:37,320
I'd rather stick to my old trade.

255
00:13:39,279 --> 00:13:41,320
Let me just lay it all out for you.

256
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,879
If my financing had gone smoothly,

257
00:13:42,879 --> 00:13:44,279
I wouldn't be turning to anyone.

258
00:13:44,279 --> 00:13:46,159
Why split a one-dollar deal in half?

259
00:13:48,559 --> 00:13:50,799
Don't you know that fund?

260
00:13:50,799 --> 00:13:52,799
The one you introduced me to last week?

261
00:13:53,120 --> 00:13:54,120
Guarantee the loan.

262
00:13:54,120 --> 00:13:56,919
I'll pay triple the bank's fixed interest.

263
00:13:57,159 --> 00:13:58,960
Plus a five percent stake of free equity.

264
00:13:58,960 --> 00:14:00,320
How's that for sincerity?

265
00:14:00,519 --> 00:14:01,679
No need to answer right away.

266
00:14:01,679 --> 00:14:02,720
Just think it over carefully.

267
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,159
Tell me once you've decided.

268
00:14:04,159 --> 00:14:05,759
You haven't brought any girls home lately.

269
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,279
Turned over a new leaf?

270
00:14:08,039 --> 00:14:09,279
What new leaf?

271
00:14:09,399 --> 00:14:11,440
Can't marry, can't live together.

272
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:13,159
You're my cautionary tale.

273
00:14:13,159 --> 00:14:15,320
You tripped, and I should jump in too?

274
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:16,320
It's just pointless.

275
00:15:08,879 --> 00:15:09,519
According to reports,

276
00:15:09,799 --> 00:15:11,720
on gifting giant pandas to Taiwan, China,

277
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:14,039
the Taiwan, China agricultural agency

278
00:15:14,039 --> 00:15:16,159
and its special panda import review task force

279
00:15:16,159 --> 00:15:17,360
recently reached a conclusion.

280
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:18,559
It was reported that

281
00:15:18,559 --> 00:15:20,120
under the island's relevant regulations,

282
00:15:20,120 --> 00:15:21,519
they cannot accept the giant pandas

283
00:15:21,519 --> 00:15:24,000
gifted by the mainland to Taiwan, China.

284
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,480
In response, various circles on the island questioned

285
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:29,039
the political meddling in this review,

286
00:15:29,039 --> 00:15:29,879
arguing that the authorities

287
00:15:29,879 --> 00:15:32,879
let politics override professionalism.

288
00:15:32,879 --> 00:15:35,039
A KMT spokesperson previously stated that

289
00:15:35,039 --> 00:15:37,159
if they block them from Taiwan, China,

290
00:15:37,159 --> 00:15:38,919
they are using a narrow ideology

291
00:15:38,919 --> 00:15:42,320
to hinder peaceful cross-strait exchanges.

292
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,399
I brought you some medicine.

293
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,559
Here you are, having to look after me.

294
00:15:57,159 --> 00:15:58,039
Don't worry about that.

295
00:15:58,039 --> 00:15:58,919
I'll just take it like this.

296
00:15:59,919 --> 00:16:00,679
I'll get you some water.

297
00:16:00,679 --> 00:16:01,639
Don't take it just yet.

298
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:13,759
Have some water.

299
00:17:14,759 --> 00:17:15,480
You're awake.

300
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:19,319
Are you feeling better?

301
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:20,799
Has your fever gone down?

302
00:17:25,279 --> 00:17:26,079
Much better.

303
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:27,680
That's good.

304
00:17:30,319 --> 00:17:31,200
Thank you.

305
00:17:44,759 --> 00:17:47,559
You didn't have to come all the way here.

306
00:17:48,799 --> 00:17:50,000
It's not like I'm going to die.

307
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:52,599
Coming here like this...

308
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,559
If I drag you down,

309
00:17:55,559 --> 00:17:57,319
will your people come after me?

310
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:00,000
I'm not worried about your anxiety.

311
00:18:00,720 --> 00:18:02,440
I'm worried you'll take the wrong meds,

312
00:18:02,640 --> 00:18:04,039
and ruin your health.

313
00:18:05,839 --> 00:18:06,960
Pregnancy is no small matter.

314
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:08,559
You have to take it seriously.

315
00:18:11,640 --> 00:18:13,480
It's not your first relationship.

316
00:18:15,359 --> 00:18:16,319
How could you be so foolish?

317
00:18:16,799 --> 00:18:18,200
Lin Kanshan should take responsibility.

318
00:18:21,039 --> 00:18:21,920
It's not his.

319
00:18:23,160 --> 00:18:25,319
I've almost forgotten what he looks like.

320
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:28,279
You thought it was his.

321
00:18:28,759 --> 00:18:30,039
Why didn't you ask me?

322
00:18:34,039 --> 00:18:35,200
That's personal.

323
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:38,960
What if it were Lin Kanshan's?

324
00:18:40,880 --> 00:18:41,880
Wouldn't you ask then either?

325
00:18:42,799 --> 00:18:44,960
I don't like forcing people.

326
00:18:49,279 --> 00:18:51,000
What do you want me to do for you?

327
00:18:55,759 --> 00:18:57,119
Why are you helping me?

328
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:59,519
Deep down, I know very well.

329
00:19:00,079 --> 00:19:01,640
Li Fengge would force me

330
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,599
to steal Wen Zongshu's bag.

331
00:19:04,400 --> 00:19:05,839
Lin Kanshan would coax me

332
00:19:06,759 --> 00:19:08,160
into taking things from the military.

333
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:13,559
Everyone has been pushing me,

334
00:19:16,119 --> 00:19:17,119
but you never did.

335
00:19:19,559 --> 00:19:21,000
I want to do something for you.

336
00:19:24,519 --> 00:19:27,799
If a police informant is arrested,

337
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:30,599
she can disclose her identity.

338
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:34,880
But if you get arrested,

339
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:38,720
neither your identity nor your ties to me

340
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:40,920
can ever be mentioned.

341
00:19:41,519 --> 00:19:42,920
Do you understand what I mean?

342
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:49,279
It's not about what you want to do for me.

343
00:19:50,319 --> 00:19:52,319
It's about what I want to do for you.

344
00:19:54,279 --> 00:19:55,279
Do you understand?

345
00:19:57,960 --> 00:20:00,440
I need you to go back, watch Lin Kanshan.

346
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:40,599
You're awake.

347
00:20:43,279 --> 00:20:44,480
Did you sleep well?

348
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,319
Not bad. You?

349
00:20:56,799 --> 00:20:57,880
Take a look for me.

350
00:20:58,400 --> 00:21:00,400
Where was Lin Kanshan these past two days?

351
00:21:01,440 --> 00:21:02,519
Though it'll have to wait a few days.

352
00:21:03,960 --> 00:21:05,200
Once I've had the abortion,

353
00:21:06,200 --> 00:21:07,359
I'll go find him.

354
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:18,839
Instant noodle time again, like clockwork.

355
00:21:18,839 --> 00:21:21,319
His routine is getting less predictable.

356
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,880
Do you think we've already

357
00:21:22,880 --> 00:21:24,720
hit a bottleneck with the wiretap?

358
00:21:24,839 --> 00:21:26,079
Who he's meeting,

359
00:21:26,079 --> 00:21:27,640
and what he's doing, we have no clue.

360
00:21:27,759 --> 00:21:29,279
You've only covered for me for a few days.

361
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:30,599
It hit a bottleneck long ago.

362
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,240
You'd better grab a drink

363
00:21:32,240 --> 00:21:33,319
and get right back to listening.

364
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,400
If you're tired, go to sleep.

365
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,079
Don't push yourself.

366
00:21:45,519 --> 00:21:46,480
I'll hold out a bit longer.

367
00:21:46,640 --> 00:21:47,599
I'll sleep at ten.

368
00:21:47,599 --> 00:21:49,240
Otherwise, I'll wake up at midnight.

369
00:21:49,319 --> 00:21:50,240
If I sleep straight through till dawn,

370
00:21:50,240 --> 00:21:51,440
my jet lag will be gone.

371
00:21:53,759 --> 00:21:56,200
I feel Ma Qi has been in touch with him.

372
00:21:56,640 --> 00:21:57,640
And quite a lot, too.

373
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,359
But we haven't caught any proof.

374
00:21:59,359 --> 00:22:00,519
Lately, Lin Kanshan

375
00:22:00,519 --> 00:22:02,559
is investing in more and more projects.

376
00:22:02,559 --> 00:22:04,640
He stays in one place less and less.

377
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:07,160
We can't exactly bug him, can we?

378
00:22:07,319 --> 00:22:08,440
With so many investments,

379
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:09,839
does he really have that much money?

380
00:22:10,839 --> 00:22:12,440
I'm helping him secure loans right now.

381
00:22:12,720 --> 00:22:14,279
Doing business can be addictive.

382
00:22:14,559 --> 00:22:16,119
Once hooked, you can't quit.

383
00:22:16,319 --> 00:22:18,480
We must monitor Lin Kanshan more closely.

384
00:22:18,599 --> 00:22:19,720
It all comes down to Qiu Tian now.

385
00:22:19,720 --> 00:22:20,799
Can she handle it?

386
00:22:20,799 --> 00:22:22,160
You think she can't?

387
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:27,359
Honestly, for Qiu Tian,

388
00:22:27,359 --> 00:22:28,960
she was just intimidated

389
00:22:28,960 --> 00:22:30,559
by state security organs.

390
00:22:30,559 --> 00:22:31,359
She's totally dazed.

391
00:22:31,359 --> 00:22:32,839
She has no idea what's really happening.

392
00:22:32,839 --> 00:22:34,640
She just agreed to this in a haze.

393
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:35,279
For her,

394
00:22:35,279 --> 00:22:36,720
she has no clue what this

395
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:38,440
will mean for her future.

396
00:22:39,079 --> 00:22:41,039
And honestly, it's the same for you.

397
00:22:41,279 --> 00:22:42,400
You don't even know

398
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:43,440
whether you should trust her.

399
00:22:43,640 --> 00:22:45,319
Like Jin Chizhong, that fake soldier,

400
00:22:45,319 --> 00:22:46,200
before he was caught,

401
00:22:46,480 --> 00:22:47,920
she never confessed to us either.

402
00:22:48,200 --> 00:22:48,960
Do you get what I mean?

403
00:22:48,960 --> 00:22:50,519
You always talk about seeing it from their side.

404
00:22:50,519 --> 00:22:51,799
I think about that too.

405
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:52,759
If I were her,

406
00:22:52,759 --> 00:22:53,920
why should I trust you?

407
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:56,519
Unless you treat me with true sincerity,

408
00:22:56,519 --> 00:22:57,960
without tricking or lying to me.

409
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,359
I'll definitely choose to trust her.

410
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:03,359
If I can't even do that,

411
00:23:03,920 --> 00:23:05,200
just like Li Fengge,

412
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:06,960
then I shouldn't be doing this job.

413
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:11,079
Wiretapping and reconnaissance...

414
00:23:11,279 --> 00:23:13,039
where you stand and your starting point

415
00:23:13,039 --> 00:23:13,880
are completely different.

416
00:23:14,279 --> 00:23:15,519
I'm just reminding you.

417
00:23:16,359 --> 00:23:18,039
Why is intelligence work so hard?

418
00:23:18,039 --> 00:23:19,240
First, the moral barrier.

419
00:23:19,240 --> 00:23:20,680
When you develop an intelligence asset,

420
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:22,319
you work with them for over a decade.

421
00:23:22,559 --> 00:23:23,640
What if the line snaps?

422
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:25,000
It's like running a marathon.

423
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,160
You run for over a decade,

424
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:27,400
near the finish line,

425
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:29,119
the road breaks, and your ankle twists.

426
00:23:29,119 --> 00:23:29,720
Put in a cast,

427
00:23:29,720 --> 00:23:30,920
you still have to keep running.

428
00:23:31,079 --> 00:23:31,880
The same goes for them,

429
00:23:31,880 --> 00:23:32,839
and for yourself.

430
00:23:32,839 --> 00:23:34,400
You know full well she's in danger,

431
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:35,480
but you have to accept it.

432
00:23:35,759 --> 00:23:37,079
If you can't make peace with that,

433
00:23:37,079 --> 00:23:38,759
your own mind will warp first.

434
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:39,640
Every time I bring this up,

435
00:23:39,640 --> 00:23:40,799
you think I'm being overdramatic.

436
00:23:40,799 --> 00:23:42,079
From a bird's-eye view,

437
00:23:42,559 --> 00:23:43,839
I'm the one who's constantly torn,

438
00:23:43,839 --> 00:23:45,079
with a knot in my heart.

439
00:23:45,079 --> 00:23:46,599
Whether it's Qiu Tian or anyone else,

440
00:23:46,599 --> 00:23:48,640
you watch them suffer,

441
00:23:48,640 --> 00:23:49,240
drinking,

442
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:50,480
sleeping around,

443
00:23:50,480 --> 00:23:51,400
wrecking themselves,

444
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:52,960
but you're powerless.

445
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:55,559
You can't interfere too much.

446
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,640
Why can't I fall asleep?

447
00:23:59,920 --> 00:24:02,319
Between sleep and waking, there's a lock.

448
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:05,720
Sometimes I can't find the key.

449
00:24:06,440 --> 00:24:08,079
Sometimes I can't open that door.

450
00:24:08,279 --> 00:24:09,519
Being cautious doesn't work.

451
00:24:09,519 --> 00:24:10,920
Being anxious doesn't work.

452
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:12,599
Day breaks,

453
00:24:13,319 --> 00:24:14,279
the door opens,

454
00:24:15,799 --> 00:24:18,440
but my mental hurdle is hard to cross.

455
00:24:23,160 --> 00:24:25,279
And there's an even greater challenge:

456
00:24:25,279 --> 00:24:27,240
How do we overcome her fear?

457
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:29,880
How do we win her political alignment?

458
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:30,880
It's not like we can drag her in

459
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:32,640
to study party-building reports together.

460
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:35,200
Intel work isn't solved in a classroom.

461
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:37,039
So when I open up to Qiu Tian,

462
00:24:37,039 --> 00:24:38,559
I must be genuinely sincere.

463
00:24:38,559 --> 00:24:39,160
I have to treat her

464
00:24:39,160 --> 00:24:41,279
as one of the most important people to me,

465
00:24:41,359 --> 00:24:43,160
as a companion in life,

466
00:24:43,160 --> 00:24:44,440
even as a partner,

467
00:24:44,720 --> 00:24:45,519
supporting each other,

468
00:24:45,519 --> 00:24:46,519
relying on each other.

469
00:24:46,720 --> 00:24:48,160
I have to see her as the person in this world

470
00:24:48,160 --> 00:24:49,240
I trust the most,

471
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:52,680
trusting her even more than myself,

472
00:24:54,920 --> 00:24:55,960
valuing her even more than myself.

473
00:25:03,519 --> 00:25:04,599
In a way,

474
00:25:05,359 --> 00:25:06,319
it has to be.

475
00:25:11,160 --> 00:25:12,839
They're almost done eating instant noodles next door.

476
00:25:13,359 --> 00:25:14,519
Keep listening.

477
00:25:59,839 --> 00:26:02,640
Investment policies must offer tangible benefits,

478
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:04,599
deliver instant results,

479
00:26:04,920 --> 00:26:06,519
and avoid hollow gimmicks.

480
00:26:06,920 --> 00:26:09,000
I am very honored to announce here

481
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:11,960
that our High-Tech Zone, by providing land

482
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:13,279
and basic utility access,

483
00:26:13,319 --> 00:26:14,440
as preferential terms,

484
00:26:14,839 --> 00:26:16,000
has officially signed

485
00:26:16,279 --> 00:26:18,319
Taiwan, China Starlight Co., Ltd.'s

486
00:26:18,319 --> 00:26:20,640
semiconductor lighting project.

487
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:23,839
Phase one requires 300 million yuan,

488
00:26:24,200 --> 00:26:26,079
taking a year and a half to build.

489
00:26:26,240 --> 00:26:28,799
Annual output may reach 2 billion yuan,

490
00:26:28,960 --> 00:26:31,680
with expected tax revenue of 280 million.

491
00:26:38,920 --> 00:26:42,079
Your brother-in-law fell out with Qian?

492
00:26:42,839 --> 00:26:44,359
They've reported each other.

493
00:26:44,519 --> 00:26:45,480
Is that true?

494
00:26:46,400 --> 00:26:47,079
Now at dinners,

495
00:26:47,079 --> 00:26:49,119
they can't even sit at the same table.

496
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:51,039
If Xie moves,

497
00:26:51,240 --> 00:26:52,680
everyone underneath moves with him.

498
00:26:52,839 --> 00:26:54,079
Naturally, some will be pleased,

499
00:26:54,079 --> 00:26:55,200
and some won't.

500
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:58,359
Annual output can reach seven billion,

501
00:26:58,359 --> 00:27:00,759
and tax revenue could reach one billion.

502
00:27:00,759 --> 00:27:02,759
I heard the boss is going to the province,

503
00:27:02,759 --> 00:27:05,000
to be chairman of the largest state firm.

504
00:27:05,200 --> 00:27:06,240
Who would have thought?

505
00:27:06,240 --> 00:27:08,000
He really is a decent man at heart.

506
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:10,519
He gets things done for the people,

507
00:27:10,519 --> 00:27:12,160
takes responsibility, and isn't corrupt.

508
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:17,759
His predecessor went down over money,

509
00:27:18,960 --> 00:27:20,200
but he held the line.

510
00:27:20,200 --> 00:27:21,400
I really respect that about him.

511
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:24,440
During demolition and urban redevelopment,

512
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:26,039
so many people tried to lobby him,

513
00:27:26,599 --> 00:27:29,039
including his secretary and family.

514
00:27:30,160 --> 00:27:31,440
Yet he still held firm.

515
00:27:31,759 --> 00:27:32,960
I genuinely admire him.

516
00:27:34,359 --> 00:27:36,200
Flies don't land on uncracked eggs.

517
00:27:36,839 --> 00:27:39,400
I believe every egg has cracks, anyway,

518
00:27:39,599 --> 00:27:41,039
or the flies are just stupid.

519
00:27:41,960 --> 00:27:44,160
Core R&D and production center

520
00:27:51,519 --> 00:27:53,000
Let's thank...

521
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,079
Mayor Xie for his wonderful speech.

522
00:27:55,279 --> 00:27:56,480
Distinguished guests,

523
00:27:56,480 --> 00:27:57,839
fellow entrepreneurs,

524
00:27:57,839 --> 00:28:00,720
the launch of Taiwan, China Starlight Co.

525
00:28:00,720 --> 00:28:02,599
is not the end of cross-Strait

526
00:28:02,599 --> 00:28:04,839
industrial cooperation for Minzhong,

527
00:28:04,839 --> 00:28:06,559
but a new beginning for win-win results...

528
00:28:06,559 --> 00:28:07,920
Whispering away...

529
00:28:08,119 --> 00:28:10,359
Who is Mr. Lin gossiping about now?

530
00:28:10,640 --> 00:28:11,799
Is he talking about me?

531
00:28:11,799 --> 00:28:13,880
The Taipei-Minzhong Chamber of Commerce

532
00:28:13,880 --> 00:28:15,880
is led by Director Wu Jinhe

533
00:28:15,880 --> 00:28:17,559
of the Development Zone.

534
00:28:17,559 --> 00:28:19,160
How would I dare step out of line?

535
00:28:21,359 --> 00:28:22,400
That project you agreed to invest in,

536
00:28:22,400 --> 00:28:23,839
are you going to invest or not?

537
00:28:24,119 --> 00:28:26,640
I've been swamped with trivial chores, Director.

538
00:28:26,960 --> 00:28:27,880
Just say the word,

539
00:28:27,880 --> 00:28:29,400
and I'll jump right to it.

540
00:28:29,400 --> 00:28:31,000
Once I finish site visits,

541
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,519
I'll report to you in person.

542
00:28:32,880 --> 00:28:34,359
You're as slippery as they come.

543
00:28:34,519 --> 00:28:36,000
Holding onto my policies,

544
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:38,440
price-shopping in Zhangzhou and Quanzhou.

545
00:28:38,759 --> 00:28:39,880
Think I don't have friends?

546
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:40,960
Think I don't get intel?

547
00:28:41,279 --> 00:28:44,079
Your shabby plant was just wasteland then.

548
00:28:44,400 --> 00:28:46,079
If I hadn't pushed you to invest,

549
00:28:46,079 --> 00:28:48,200
would it be the park's prime core now?

550
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:48,920
Yes, yes, of course.

551
00:28:48,920 --> 00:28:50,200
Where do you plan to invest next?

552
00:28:50,759 --> 00:28:52,160
By the planned airport.

553
00:28:53,039 --> 00:28:54,279
Right now,

554
00:28:54,279 --> 00:28:55,960
I borrow from Brother Xiao every day.

555
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:56,839
He knows best.

556
00:28:57,039 --> 00:28:58,759
I don't have a single penny left.

557
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:00,480
I can only look for bargains.

558
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:03,240
I'll invest wherever the land is cheapest.

559
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:06,480
...elevates Minzhong's city brand value,

560
00:29:06,599 --> 00:29:11,039
and deepens our bond in prospering together.

561
00:29:15,319 --> 00:29:16,880
With so many good spots, you picked none,

562
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,480
insisting on the outskirts instead.

563
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:20,160
It's right near the dual-use airport.

564
00:29:20,480 --> 00:29:22,559
Anyone can tell it's way too remote.

565
00:29:22,559 --> 00:29:24,200
I really don't get what you're thinking.

566
00:29:24,200 --> 00:29:26,079
I can relocate my current plant there.

567
00:29:26,079 --> 00:29:27,400
Hiring workers is easier there anyway.

568
00:29:27,400 --> 00:29:28,839
Then tear down the old workshops

569
00:29:28,839 --> 00:29:29,799
and build commercial residences.

570
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:31,000
Brother,

571
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:32,960
if a single word I said was a lie,

572
00:29:32,960 --> 00:29:34,079
may I twist my ankle walking out the door.

573
00:29:34,720 --> 00:29:36,640
I know what you're plotting.

574
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:39,000
Then give it to me straight.

575
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:40,880
Is this actually possible or not?

576
00:29:42,480 --> 00:29:43,720
Let me put it this way.

577
00:29:44,799 --> 00:29:47,160
Investment promotion is skilled work.

578
00:29:47,160 --> 00:29:48,880
You have to have real experience.

579
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:50,640
You can't just blindly obey leaders either,

580
00:29:50,640 --> 00:29:53,240
or novices will boss around experts,

581
00:29:53,480 --> 00:29:54,799
and things will go downhill.

582
00:29:54,799 --> 00:29:55,119
Of course,

583
00:29:55,119 --> 00:29:57,279
leaders won't stay silent either.

584
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:59,680
So you must learn how to present reports.

585
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:03,039
Any proposal you submit

586
00:30:03,039 --> 00:30:05,720
will circle back to me anyway.

587
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:07,079
It must be feasible,

588
00:30:07,240 --> 00:30:08,200
and it must be solid.

589
00:30:24,799 --> 00:30:26,160
You know what I mean, right?

590
00:30:26,799 --> 00:30:27,640
You know what I mean?

591
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:28,519
I get it.

592
00:30:28,519 --> 00:30:30,359
Either way, I'm counting on you, buddy.

593
00:30:30,359 --> 00:30:31,279
Counting on you.

594
00:30:32,319 --> 00:30:33,079
I'm done eating.

595
00:30:33,920 --> 00:30:34,839
Then in a bit, let's go

596
00:30:34,839 --> 00:30:35,799
weigh down that roll-up banner,

597
00:30:35,799 --> 00:30:36,799
so the wind doesn't blow it away.

598
00:30:36,799 --> 00:30:37,480
No problem.

599
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:51,480
Straits International Travel Agency.

600
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:53,359
Going international now.

601
00:30:54,240 --> 00:30:56,200
You're working with Jinlan.

602
00:30:58,559 --> 00:30:59,720
Why are you here?

603
00:31:02,480 --> 00:31:03,839
You're attending this forum, too?

604
00:31:04,240 --> 00:31:06,079
I go to any forum you attend.

605
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:12,359
Nothing more to it.

606
00:31:13,039 --> 00:31:14,599
I just wanted to take you out for a meal.

607
00:31:15,119 --> 00:31:16,960
There are a few things I'd like to ask your advice on.

608
00:31:19,279 --> 00:31:21,200
If there's anything, just say it right here.

609
00:31:22,839 --> 00:31:25,599
Is your aunt still in Jiangxi?

610
00:31:57,759 --> 00:31:58,640
Heading east on Jiefang Road,

611
00:31:58,640 --> 00:32:00,359
at the first light past the alcohol plant,

612
00:32:00,359 --> 00:32:01,559
right as the light turned yellow to red,

613
00:32:01,559 --> 00:32:02,920
running that light was a decent move.

614
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:04,640
If your timing had been just a bit sharper,

615
00:32:04,640 --> 00:32:05,720
you would've lost me.

616
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:07,359
Still wasn't sharp enough.

617
00:32:07,480 --> 00:32:08,839
I didn't expect that while crossing,

618
00:32:08,839 --> 00:32:10,480
that truck would suddenly slow down.

619
00:32:11,559 --> 00:32:12,680
If it had kept driving normally,

620
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:13,960
it probably would've blocked you off.

621
00:32:14,319 --> 00:32:16,359
Since when are truck drivers so courteous?

622
00:32:17,640 --> 00:32:18,599
No need to be modest.

623
00:32:18,599 --> 00:32:19,640
For someone your age,

624
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:21,720
your tailing skills are solid in our unit.

625
00:32:21,720 --> 00:32:23,279
Many people never realize in their lives

626
00:32:23,279 --> 00:32:25,160
driving skill isn't key in tailing.

627
00:32:25,599 --> 00:32:26,839
Brains matter most.

628
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:27,759
Of course,

629
00:32:27,759 --> 00:32:29,319
office politics is another story.

630
00:32:29,759 --> 00:32:31,039
Baoshan made deputy division head by now, right?

631
00:32:32,119 --> 00:32:33,599
Director Wu is retiring soon.

632
00:32:33,599 --> 00:32:34,440
You definitely know.

633
00:32:36,119 --> 00:32:37,279
Still beating around the bush with me?

634
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:39,319
Is Baoshan's promotion supposed to be a secret?

635
00:32:39,759 --> 00:32:41,000
Even if I wanted to take this intel

636
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:42,039
and sell it to Taiwan, China,

637
00:32:42,359 --> 00:32:43,720
would it even buy me a bowl of rice noodles?

638
00:32:44,359 --> 00:32:46,440
You're so sharp, you know everything.

639
00:32:46,440 --> 00:32:47,680
So don't ask me.

640
00:32:49,680 --> 00:32:50,759
Once Wu Shenglai retires,

641
00:32:50,759 --> 00:32:52,079
Old Wei will definitely take over.

642
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:54,519
Though you're not a reserve cadre,

643
00:32:54,839 --> 00:32:56,480
getting promoted to team leader or deputy

644
00:32:56,480 --> 00:32:57,359
shouldn't be much of a problem.

645
00:32:58,720 --> 00:33:00,759
Me, I just do my job.

646
00:33:00,759 --> 00:33:02,880
Promotions don't matter that much to me.

647
00:33:03,599 --> 00:33:04,559
You don't mean that.

648
00:33:05,160 --> 00:33:06,880
Still haven't changed after all these years.

649
00:33:06,880 --> 00:33:07,960
Still giving me the runaround.

650
00:33:10,200 --> 00:33:11,720
This batch of intel didn't come easy.

651
00:33:11,720 --> 00:33:12,799
When the new chief takes office,

652
00:33:12,799 --> 00:33:14,160
let him make a big splash,

653
00:33:14,160 --> 00:33:16,319
and get them to approve more funding.

654
00:33:16,319 --> 00:33:17,480
Don't be so stingy.

655
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:19,359
Let's not look worse off than Taiwan, China.

656
00:33:20,160 --> 00:33:22,039
A new chief means a lot of work.

657
00:33:22,039 --> 00:33:23,559
I've been swamped with odds and ends every day.

658
00:33:23,559 --> 00:33:25,160
How's the opening of your new company going?

659
00:33:25,160 --> 00:33:26,880
I've been too busy lately to drop by.

660
00:33:27,039 --> 00:33:28,000
To be honest,

661
00:33:28,000 --> 00:33:29,519
doing investments and running a business

662
00:33:29,519 --> 00:33:32,000
is harder than intel or turning an asset.

663
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:36,200
I bought this bag with my own money on a business trip.

664
00:33:36,359 --> 00:33:37,200
The red envelope is inside too.

665
00:33:37,480 --> 00:33:38,200
Happy birthday.

666
00:33:41,519 --> 00:33:42,799
I never celebrate birthdays.

667
00:33:42,799 --> 00:33:43,920
Between all the real and fake identities,

668
00:33:43,920 --> 00:33:45,359
I don't even know what day I was born anymore.

669
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:48,000
Still,

670
00:33:49,200 --> 00:33:49,960
thank you anyway.

671
00:33:51,839 --> 00:33:52,319
By the way,

672
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:55,680
Chen Shui-bian's family corruption scandal

673
00:33:55,680 --> 00:33:57,000
is blowing up bigger by the day.

674
00:33:57,000 --> 00:33:59,000
His approval rating has hit rock bottom,

675
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:01,000
and his grip on the party has weakened.

676
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:01,920
To protect himself,

677
00:34:01,920 --> 00:34:03,359
he's sure to push for radical independence.

678
00:34:03,599 --> 00:34:04,599
Got any intel?

679
00:34:04,680 --> 00:34:05,319
The more, the better.

680
00:34:05,400 --> 00:34:07,000
Reforms and the UN membership referendum—

681
00:34:07,119 --> 00:34:08,559
that's basically all out in the open.

682
00:34:08,559 --> 00:34:09,559
Nothing special about it.

683
00:34:09,920 --> 00:34:11,159
The higher-ups want

684
00:34:11,280 --> 00:34:13,079
you to use your overseas business

685
00:34:13,239 --> 00:34:14,920
to dig up more detailed intelligence.

686
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:17,159
Like dates and places for A-bian's plans,

687
00:34:17,199 --> 00:34:18,079
things like that.

688
00:34:18,840 --> 00:34:20,280
Go back and tell your boss

689
00:34:20,760 --> 00:34:22,199
that they and I are divorced.

690
00:34:22,199 --> 00:34:24,199
Right now, at most, you and I are casually dating.

691
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:25,199
Asking is fine,

692
00:34:25,840 --> 00:34:26,679
so don't give me orders.

693
00:34:28,039 --> 00:34:29,559
Divorce or not, feelings linger.

694
00:34:29,639 --> 00:34:31,039
We know each other inside and out.

695
00:34:31,039 --> 00:34:33,280
Only an ex-wife dares to be so blunt.

696
00:34:33,360 --> 00:34:34,320
Much appreciated, Boss Ma.

697
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:28,960
Okay, thank you.

698
00:35:29,199 --> 00:35:30,159
Enjoy your meal, sir.

699
00:36:05,400 --> 00:36:06,159
Welcome.

700
00:36:06,159 --> 00:36:06,880
Right this way, please.

701
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:35,039
It's so windy outside.

702
00:36:35,880 --> 00:36:37,239
My hair is all messed up.

703
00:36:40,519 --> 00:36:41,480
Mutton hotpot?

704
00:36:43,800 --> 00:36:45,679
Does it taste like what we had in Beijing?

705
00:36:47,039 --> 00:36:47,960
I heard it's really good,

706
00:36:48,639 --> 00:36:49,840
so I booked this place specifically.

707
00:36:51,039 --> 00:36:51,599
Try some.

708
00:36:52,800 --> 00:36:54,760
See if it's any different from Beijing.

709
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:56,199
Here, have a bite.

710
00:36:56,199 --> 00:36:58,280
The dipping sauce is made Beijing-style, too.

711
00:36:58,400 --> 00:36:59,440
Quite a spread.

712
00:36:59,760 --> 00:37:01,239
Just how big a deal do you want to talk about?

713
00:37:08,159 --> 00:37:10,679
There's a Dayu County in Ganzhou, Jiangxi.

714
00:37:10,679 --> 00:37:12,159
There are tungsten mines in the mountains.

715
00:37:12,639 --> 00:37:13,559
Either way,

716
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:15,400
Aunt knows the area well.

717
00:37:15,559 --> 00:37:16,599
I'd like to ask for her help.

718
00:37:17,159 --> 00:37:18,639
She can name her consulting fee.

719
00:37:19,119 --> 00:37:19,960
I won't haggle at all.

720
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:24,039
It's not bad.

721
00:37:24,639 --> 00:37:26,199
I haven't had mutton hotpot in years.

722
00:37:29,119 --> 00:37:29,719
Are you done?

723
00:37:34,960 --> 00:37:36,239
There's one more thing.

724
00:37:38,360 --> 00:37:39,840
I'd like you to come back to the company.

725
00:37:40,679 --> 00:37:42,000
You can choose any position you want.

726
00:37:42,559 --> 00:37:43,559
Even part-time is fine.

727
00:37:44,320 --> 00:37:45,480
Business is business.

728
00:37:46,039 --> 00:37:47,440
Strictly money, no feelings involved.

729
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:53,840
Then I guessed wrong.

730
00:37:58,079 --> 00:38:01,079
I thought you wanted to talk about feelings.

731
00:38:14,519 --> 00:38:15,960
I was worried if we rushed the talk,

732
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:17,519
I'd scare you off.

733
00:38:22,599 --> 00:38:23,599
Let's take our time with the drinks,

734
00:38:23,840 --> 00:38:24,800
and talk things through slowly.

735
00:38:34,280 --> 00:38:35,320
Come on, have some food.

736
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:37,400
Come, have some lamb.

737
00:38:37,840 --> 00:38:39,079
Take your time, no rush.

738
00:38:40,480 --> 00:38:42,400
You know, joining the World Trade Organization...

739
00:38:42,400 --> 00:38:43,360
is no joke.

740
00:38:44,199 --> 00:38:45,679
The potential of China's economy

741
00:38:45,679 --> 00:38:47,079
is beyond your imagination.

742
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:48,320
I'm definitely going all in.

743
00:38:48,519 --> 00:38:50,960
So, garment factories, toy factories...

744
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:51,840
I'm dropping all of that.

745
00:38:52,280 --> 00:38:54,239
I'll focus entirely on real estate,

746
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:56,199
just acquiring land and building properties.

747
00:38:56,199 --> 00:38:57,320
Once the first project is done,

748
00:38:57,320 --> 00:38:59,480
I can mortgage it to the bank for loans,

749
00:38:59,679 --> 00:39:01,239
and immediately jump into the next one.

750
00:39:05,519 --> 00:39:06,519
Just like that.

751
00:39:17,800 --> 00:39:18,400
But

752
00:39:20,159 --> 00:39:21,840
I've just moved too fast,

753
00:39:22,920 --> 00:39:23,760
and spread myself a bit thin.

754
00:39:24,960 --> 00:39:26,239
I even want to get into tungsten mining down the road.

755
00:39:27,119 --> 00:39:27,880
So,

756
00:39:29,119 --> 00:39:30,360
I need someone who can help me.

757
00:39:33,639 --> 00:39:36,079
I really need one of my own people to help me.

758
00:39:46,960 --> 00:39:48,239
Name your salary.

759
00:39:48,639 --> 00:39:49,679
You can start tomorrow.

760
00:40:03,440 --> 00:40:04,440
Hello, Mr. Lin.

761
00:40:05,199 --> 00:40:07,760
This is my assistant, Jin Lina.

762
00:40:07,840 --> 00:40:08,719
Get acquainted.

763
00:40:08,719 --> 00:40:10,039
Hello, Secretary Jin.

764
00:40:10,119 --> 00:40:11,119
Hello, everyone.

765
00:40:11,159 --> 00:40:11,679
Over here.

766
00:40:18,000 --> 00:40:19,119
This is your desk.

767
00:40:20,480 --> 00:40:21,679
It was just set up.

768
00:40:22,440 --> 00:40:23,400
A brand-new nameplate,

769
00:40:24,119 --> 00:40:25,880
and the cushion is new too.

770
00:40:25,920 --> 00:40:26,920
Don't you always have back pain?

771
00:40:27,039 --> 00:40:28,599
Sitting on that will be more comfortable.

772
00:40:30,159 --> 00:40:31,880
My office is right next door.

773
00:40:32,039 --> 00:40:33,719
I can just call out and you'll hear me.

774
00:40:35,880 --> 00:40:38,159
Come take a look at my office.

775
00:40:44,320 --> 00:40:44,920
All these...

776
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:48,159
are things I've collected

777
00:40:48,239 --> 00:40:49,599
over the years—all treasures.

778
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:51,400
Everything over here too.

779
00:40:52,840 --> 00:40:53,440
So...

780
00:40:53,679 --> 00:40:55,519
have someone come tidy up regularly.

781
00:40:55,519 --> 00:40:57,400
But you must be extremely careful.

782
00:40:59,320 --> 00:40:59,920
Come.

783
00:41:00,639 --> 00:41:02,159
Look at our new property development.

784
00:41:02,719 --> 00:41:04,039
Tell me what you think.

785
00:41:06,079 --> 00:41:07,039
Very impressive!

786
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:08,840
We're growing bigger and stronger.

787
00:41:10,360 --> 00:41:13,320
There's a lot of stuff on that computer.

788
00:41:13,960 --> 00:41:14,760
Don't touch it.

789
00:41:15,119 --> 00:41:16,880
If it's moved, I won't be able to find anything.

790
00:41:29,639 --> 00:41:30,079
By the way,

791
00:41:30,760 --> 00:41:31,239
over here.

792
00:41:38,239 --> 00:41:40,519
All the cigarettes, liquor, and tea are here.

793
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:42,960
If important guests come by,

794
00:41:43,159 --> 00:41:45,280
offer Chunghwa cigarettes and fine tea.

795
00:41:45,519 --> 00:41:46,639
For regular guests,

796
00:41:46,639 --> 00:41:48,199
Yuxi cigarettes will do.

797
00:41:48,719 --> 00:41:50,079
Still as stingy as ever, aren't you?

798
00:41:50,320 --> 00:41:51,719
Well, that's how money is saved.

799
00:41:54,199 --> 00:41:56,480
Oh, and that power outlet is broken.

800
00:41:56,559 --> 00:41:57,760
It was broken when they installed it.

801
00:41:58,000 --> 00:42:00,039
Remember to get someone to fix it.

802
00:42:01,119 --> 00:42:03,079
We've signed a lot of new contracts lately.

803
00:42:03,159 --> 00:42:04,559
Both old and new,

804
00:42:04,599 --> 00:42:06,719
all the contracts and files are over here.

805
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:07,840
It's a little messy,

806
00:42:08,360 --> 00:42:10,039
so you'll need to take some time

807
00:42:10,039 --> 00:42:11,400
to sort it all out.

808
00:42:11,880 --> 00:42:12,519
Thanks for your hard work.

809
00:42:17,480 --> 00:42:19,119
Your company has changed completely.

810
00:42:19,320 --> 00:42:20,960
You're really expanding fast.

811
00:42:21,199 --> 00:42:22,199
Everything's moving so quickly,

812
00:42:22,960 --> 00:42:24,159
I'm worried I won't be able to keep up.

813
00:42:24,400 --> 00:42:25,679
You'll do fine.

814
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:28,079
You're capable and sharp.

815
00:42:28,159 --> 00:42:30,079
You'll get the hang of it in no time.

816
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:32,360
Working with Jinlan all these years,

817
00:42:32,639 --> 00:42:34,679
you must be even better with people now.

818
00:42:34,920 --> 00:42:36,079
You could easily be a general manager.

819
00:42:36,159 --> 00:42:36,719
Am I right?

820
00:42:37,559 --> 00:42:39,400
The travel agency has hundreds of staff.

821
00:42:39,599 --> 00:42:41,239
Jinlan usually handled her work,

822
00:42:41,320 --> 00:42:42,599
and I handled mine.

823
00:42:42,920 --> 00:42:43,880
We didn't interact much.

824
00:42:46,639 --> 00:42:48,559
I'll take the call myself.

825
00:42:51,239 --> 00:42:52,440
Hello, go ahead.

826
00:42:54,000 --> 00:42:54,920
Hold on a second.

827
00:42:56,719 --> 00:42:57,840
Could you step outside for a moment?

828
00:43:08,440 --> 00:43:09,519
I'm Wang Kai,

829
00:43:09,519 --> 00:43:11,239
inviting you to watch the drama

830
00:43:11,239 --> 00:43:12,079
*Confrontation*.

831
00:43:12,440 --> 00:43:13,760
Before you enter a room,

832
00:43:13,880 --> 00:43:15,880
you must have a picture in your mind:

833
